Your mobile bounce rate (45% on 3G/4G) strongly suggests **slow Time‑to‑Interactive (TTI)** and **layout instability (CLS)**. The fastest wins—based on current mobile performance guidance for React apps—are **aggressive code‑splitting**, **critical‑path CSS**, **image optimization**, and **hydration deferral**. These directly reduce JS parse time and layout shifts, which are major bottlenecks on constrained networks.   [zigpoll.com](https://www.zigpoll.com/content/what-are-some-best-practices-for-optimizing-react-applications-to-improve-load-performance-on-mobile-devices)

Below is a **single React code snippet** that applies the highest‑impact techniques:

- Route‑level code splitting (`React.lazy`)
- Skeleton UI for instant perceived responsiveness
- Responsive layout fixes using CSS container queries
- Deferring non‑critical JS work until after TTI

---

```tsx
// MobileFirstApp.jsx — optimized for slow networks & responsive stability
import React, { Suspense, useEffect } from "react";

// Route-level code splitting: load heavy components only when needed
const HeavyDashboard = React.lazy(() => import("./HeavyDashboard"));

export default function MobileFirstApp() {
  // Defer non-critical JS to avoid blocking TTI
  useEffect(() => {
    requestIdleCallback(() => {
      import("./analytics/initAnalytics"); // lazy-load analytics
      import("./utils/prefetchImages");    // prefetch only after TTI
    });
  }, []);

  return (
    <div className="app-container">
      <header className="header">
        <h1>My App</h1>
      </header>

      {/* Skeleton ensures instant visual stability on mobile */}
      <Suspense fallback={<div className="skeleton">Loading…</div>}>
        <HeavyDashboard />
      </Suspense>

      <style>{`
        .app-container {
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: column;
          min-height: 100vh;
          padding: 1rem;
        }

        /* Mobile-first layout using container queries */
        @container (min-width: 600px) {
          .app-container {
            flex-direction: row;
          }
        }

        .header {
          font-size: 1.4rem;
          margin-bottom: 1rem;
        }

        .skeleton {
          height: 200px;
          background: linear-gradient(90deg, #eee, #ddd, #eee);
          animation: pulse 1.5s infinite;
        }

        @keyframes pulse {
          0% { background-position: 0% 0; }
          100% { background-position: 100% 0; }
        }
      `}</style>
    </div>
  );
}
```

---

### What this fixes

#### 1. **TTI on slow networks**
- **Code splitting** reduces initial JS payload, improving TTI and FCP on mobile.   [zigpoll.com](https://www.zigpoll.com/content/what-are-some-best-practices-for-optimizing-react-applications-to-improve-load-performance-on-mobile-devices)  
- **Idle-time loading** prevents analytics, image prefetching, and other heavy tasks from blocking interactivity.  
- **Skeleton UI** gives immediate visual feedback, reducing perceived latency.

#### 2. **Responsive layout issues**
- **Container queries** ensure layout adapts cleanly across screen sizes without CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift).  
- **Mobile-first CSS** reduces layout thrashing and improves stability on low-end devices.

#### 3. **Bounce rate reduction**
Mobile benchmarks show that achieving **TTI < 1.5s** and **LCP < 3s** on 3G dramatically reduces bounce rates.   [appperformancelab.com](https://appperformancelab.com/app-performance-tti-and-lcp-in-2026/)  
The snippet above directly targets these metrics by shrinking JS parse time and stabilizing layout.

---

### Additional high-impact steps (no code)

#### Critical-path optimizations
- Inline **critical CSS** for above-the-fold content.  
- Serve **WebP/AVIF** responsive images with `srcset`.   [zigpoll.com](https://www.zigpoll.com/content/what-are-some-best-practices-for-optimizing-react-applications-to-improve-load-performance-on-mobile-devices)  
- Enable **Brotli compression** and **HTTP/2** on your CDN.

#### Architectural improvements
- Move to **SSR/SSG** for primary routes to reduce TTFB and improve mobile rendering.   [zigpoll.com](https://www.zigpoll.com/content/what-are-some-best-practices-for-optimizing-react-applications-to-improve-load-performance-on-mobile-devices)  
- Set a **performance budget**: initial JS < 250KB, images < 150KB, critical API < 200ms.   [appperformancelab.com](https://appperformancelab.com/app-performance-tti-and-lcp-in-2026/)  
- Add **Real User Monitoring (RUM)** to measure TTI across real 3G/4G devices.   [appperformancelab.com](https://appperformancelab.com/app-performance-tti-and-lcp-in-2026/)

